libjq-xs-perl (2.00-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
  * Embed jq 1.8.2 instead of linking the libjq the distribution packages;
    drop the libjq-dev build dependency.  The package no longer depends on
    libjq1 at runtime, and the jq filter semantics no longer vary with the
    suite's jq version.
  * Record the licenses of the vendored jq, decNumber and oniguruma, and
    install THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.
  * Expose more of the libjq API: named and positional arguments, jq's
    output formatting options, halt/halt_error, the debug, stderr and
    input/inputs builtins, jq attributes, and JSON parsing and printing
    helpers.
  * New allow_includes option refuses filters containing include or import,
    for callers compiling programs they did not write.

 -- James Rouzier <rouzier@gmail.com>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

